# DaisyUI tooltips on icon-only buttons

Every button that shows **only an icon** (no visible text label) must use a DaisyUI tooltip so the action is discoverable on hover/focus.

## Required pattern

Wrap the button (or put tooltip classes on a parent) and set `data-tip`. Keep `aria-label` in sync for accessibility.

```svelte
<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<div class="tooltip tooltip-right" data-tip="Brush (B)">
  <button type="button" class="btn btn-square btn-xs" aria-label="Brush (B)">
    <Brush class="h-4 w-4" />
  </button>
</div>

<!-- ✅ GOOD (tooltip on the control itself when supported) -->
<button
  type="button"
  class="btn btn-square btn-xs tooltip"
  data-tip="Delete layer"
  aria-label="Delete layer"
>
  <Trash2 class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
</button>
```

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD — native title only, or no tip -->
<button type="button" class="btn btn-square" title="Brush">
  <Brush class="h-4 w-4" />
</button>
```

## Rules

- Prefer DaisyUI `tooltip` + `data-tip` over the HTML `title` attribute for icon-only controls
- Choose placement when needed: `tooltip-right`, `tooltip-left`, `tooltip-top`, `tooltip-bottom`
- Text-labeled buttons (visible words inside the button) do **not** require a tooltip
- Toolbar / square icon buttons in the image editor and elsewhere must follow this every time you add one
